rota lap 5240, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; listening for the page nobody answered, and REDS %767's second field was it
think Read the card whole, the claim board, and the OPEN ledger rows. Three of my lane's rows want Keaton's word -- %767 %765 %756 -- and the agent-doable queue's first two were claimed by copal and folded.
think The aether reading asks what the work is saying underneath the words. %767's second field says outright: nothing in this tree asks whether every field a contract publishes carries a ceiling that contract declares. A whole-tree grep found no such reader. That is a page nobody answered, and it is squarely the receipt-contract seam.
think Checked absence with path_absence_scan before assuming the instrument was missing, opened a claim naming the three files, and pushed it before building.
think The reading holds three documents to one answer: the contract's ceiling table, the bounds module's max_* constants, and every _refusal( call in the admission module. Field names come from a string literal, from the array entries a loop consumes, or -- for encoded_fact and receipt_facts -- read out of the refusal record rather than spelled twice.
think Gated unnamed_ceiling and value_disagrees at zero. Reported population_undeclared, borrowed_rows and row_unenforced, each a thing a lawful contract does today, because enumerating a population changes what the product publishes and that returns to Keaton.
obs My first draft stripped a call's arguments at the line's FIRST paren, which is the enclosing if (, so eight of fourteen sites vanished and the reading still looked plausible at six. It is a planted mutation now.
obs My first bite detector watched the site count alone and called two of three mutations harmless -- losing the population rescue moves named and unnamed and leaves sites exactly where it stood. The detector reads all four gated numbers now.
obs The control's exit-status probes died silently under set -e inside command substitution, so a refusing scan read as an empty answer rather than a failing one. Rewritten as if/then/else.
obs THREE WITHDRAWALS IN ONE HOUR, ONE CAUSE. The hot pass red led to Rishi's if claiming the else that belongs to assert -- rishi/src/main.rye do_if reads all right of the first top-level " else " as the ELSE STATEMENT, so if (C) then assert X else "msg" runs the assert stripped of its message when C holds and returns error.UnknownStatement when it does not. Booked %804, trimmed four times against a pin 50 bytes under its bound, folded %802 for room. The final rebase answered every part: a peer had folded %802 forty minutes earlier, upstream had booked %804 through %808, and %806 -- stamped 20260917.030908, sixteen minutes before mine -- had booked the same defect, same line, same pen. Fold withdrawn, row renumbered %809, row withdrawn whole.
obs THE HALF %806 DOES NOT CARRY is the true branch: the assert runs without its message, so a real failure prints the expression where the author's sentence should stand. Proven in a four-line pen. 9 sites across 7 living .rish files. Carried on my shelf account for whoever takes the repair.
obs THE GAP THIS COST: the baton asks a lap to claim a new instrument or a BOOKED red. It asks nothing about a red the lap is about to BOOK, or a fold it is about to take -- the two most collision-prone acts in this fleet, since every ship reads the same pin at each lap open. My claim named its three instrument files honestly and covered none of the three things that collided.
obs Five reds stood on the hot pass and every one predates this lap, proven by re-running each with the lap's own work stashed and reading the same numbers: unheard_guard control_unheard=20 against a ceiling of 18, law_guard_heard refused behind it, instrument_refusal swallowed_instrument_passes=2 against zero with both lines in tools/fixtures/b/kyri_resins_landed_scan.sh, built_tool_freshness stale_tool, and ryekey through %804. Surfaced on the card rather than repaired -- each belongs to the lane that landed it, and taking a peer's freshly landed ceiling is what the claim board exists to prevent.
obs My control used sed -i thirteen times, which shell_dialect gates at zero as a GNU extension; rewritten as an edit helper writing through the original file, which is also what preserves a tracked mode.
obs The cold endurance run was launched at lap open and its verdict fixed at tree_moved once the claim commit landed, so it was stopped through tools/f/fleet_call.sh --signal TERM rather than by name.
